<div id="2026-09-05-git-merge-uncommitted-todo" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-05 — git_merge auto-todo for uncommitted_on_main (precondition blocker)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>ROOT CAUSE.</strong> merge_to_main (from 3d worktree UI :4003) correctly resolved primary main checkout via main_repo_path + explicit {repo}, ran status --porcelain on it, then git merge --no-ff '3d' failed because main had uncommitted changes (dirty: Root.pm, User.pm, Weather.pm, register.tt, 2026-08-31 changelog inc). merge_branch classified as reason=uncommitted_on_main (is_main_target true), provided good error_msg + fix_hint, but *unconditionally* logged the full failure detail at 'error' level (Git.pm:1835). Logging.pm + ErrorAudit turns ERROR into auto-audit todo (even for expected user-fixable precondition like "main dirty — commit/stash on primary first").</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>DO.</strong> Lower log level for known precondition blocks (uncommitted_*, worktree_collision, merge_in_progress, conflict, missing_ref) to 'warn' inside merge_branch so they do not generate audit todos. Keep real/unexpected failures at 'error'. UI already handles uncommitted_on_main specially and points to primary. Use only app git paths (main_repo_path + explicit repo override; never checkout main in worktree). Pre-flight status on target remains in merge_branch.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>DO NOT.</strong> Hand-edit the primary or worktree .git; bypass the dirty check; log precondition failures as ERROR; close todo without evidence that main was cleaned and merge retried successfully (or documented non-repro after cleanup).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>ACCEPT.</strong> Root cause matches log exactly (reason=uncommitted_on_main, dirty files listed, detail= the git "would be overwritten" + "Merge with strategy ort failed"). Verified: perl -c Git.pm + Admin/Git.pm clean; code review of merge_branch (pre-flight porcelain at 1696, classification 1760-1787, log at 1844 now conditional); controller merge_to_main downgrades appropriately. The merge *should* have failed; the bug was the ERROR log + todo for a documented precondition. CODER_READY (no re-plan for similar log-level precondition cases).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Util/Git.pm:1835 (log level) + 1693 (pre-flight)</code>, <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm:1844 (caller level)</code>, <code>Comserv/root/static/js/git-dashboard.js</code> (client handling), new changelog entry.</p>
</div>